---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Sergi Romero" description="About Sergi Romero: robotics and automation engineer.">
  <main>
    <h1>About</h1>

    <section aria-labelledby="profile-heading">
      <h2 id="profile-heading">Profile</h2>
      <p>
        Robotics and automation engineer with a strong interest in artificial
        intelligence, neural networks, machine learning and research. I
        like building systems that combine robotics with sensing, control and
        data-driven methods — and I value being able to explain the engineering
        decisions behind them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="education-heading">
      <h2 id="education-heading">Education</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>M.Sc. in Robotics and Automatic Control</strong> — Universitat
          Politècnica de Catalunya (UPC), ETSEIB
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>B.Sc. in Industrial Electronic Engineering and Electronics</strong> —
          Universitat Politècnica de Catalunya (UPC), EEBE
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
      <h2 id="experience-heading">Experience</h2>

      <div class="job">
        <h3>Universal Robots (UR) — R&amp;D Software, Student Worker</h3>
        <p class="job-meta">Odense, Denmark · Master's internship · ~6 months</p>
        <p>
          Worked in the team behind the UR external control / driver stack. Built
          the official <a
            href="https://github.com/UniversalRobots/RTDE_ROS2_Publisher"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >RTDE_ROS2_Publisher</a
          >
          package from scratch, and contributed across the
          <a
            href="https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_Client_Library"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >client library</a
          >
          and the
          <a
            href="https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_ROS2_Driver"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >ROS2 driver</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>What I worked on:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>URScript</strong> — scripting on the robot side, including the
            external control URScript and real-time communication setup.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>RTDE (Real-Time Data Exchange)</strong> — real-time data
            streaming; authored the RTDE_ROS2_Publisher package.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>UR Cap (U+ / ucap) with Angular</strong> — designed a UR Cap,
            a front-end extension that runs on the teach pendant.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Client library &amp; driver</strong> — sockets, threads,
            real-time scheduling (FIFO) for the RTDE thread, payload handling, tool
            communication refactor, and more.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Testing &amp; quality</strong> — unit tests, integration
            coverage, CI workflows and debugging across the stack.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="note">
          My open-source work during this internship is public on
          <a
            href="https://github.com/srvald"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >github.com/srvald</a
          >, including merged pull requests in the UR ROS stack.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <h3>Mobile Industrial Robots (MIR) — Technical Engineer</h3>
        <p class="job-meta">Intern, then part-time · UK &amp; Ireland · ~2 years</p>
        <p>
          Worked in technical service while studying, gaining hands-on knowledge of
          the hardware. Responsibilities included:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Hardware</strong> — repairing robots and understanding the
            physical system.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Networks &amp; diagnostics</strong> — networking, and
            analysing the robot's software: ROS topics, nodes, and
            <code>rosout</code> logs to find failures.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>REST API</strong> — building small applications on the MIR
            REST API.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>